  ('zcrm_1579374000104541003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442195', 'Kristin Smith', NULL, 'Kristin called into the concierge here today and unfortunately she was bit by a Deer Tick up where she is in WI. She said after about a week or so, she started feeling crappy and went to the Urgent Care to get tested for Lymes Disease. She came back positive. She then was referred to have a few more blood tests done and is now getting her $2500 bill in the mail. I explained to her that for this exact type of situation, she is ONLY to pay her IUA of $1k and that is it. She is to then keep and get her receipts that show proof of the $1k IUA payment, and then submit those and the rest of the billing into Zion Health. They will start a Need case and set her up with a case worker that will walk her through everything. After her IUA is met, Zion will share the rest of the costs associated with this Need. Zion will pay the provider(s) directly and negotiate everything on her behalf. I sent her the How to submit a Need to Zion email, and highly suggested she call Zion after she got off the phone with me to explain everything and start the Need, since she has the bills now, now is the perfect time. She was thrilled how easy this is and I was able to relate to her as I have Lymes myself. She feels a LOT better now and all her worries are gone she stated. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-09-30 09:35:03', '2022-09-30 09:35:03'),
