  ('zcrm_1579374000103910032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000009614029', 'Kathryn Tagenel', NULL, '9-23-2022:  Kathy called.  She was trying to get into her "portal" to see everything she has.  We walked thru a lot.  She''s on an older Sedera plan & I can see it looks time sensitive for her to set-up the new Sedera info by 10/1/22.  She''ll contact Charlie right away for help (& she''s out of town next week).  
     - I tried to get into her MPB.Health portal & it''s not allowing me in.  But she had clicked on "forgot my pw", so I told her we can try again soon.  Then showed her the ''Memb Updates'' items (she''s not needing anything now, just thought she could go & see everything her plan includes in her portal). 
     - We talked about:  = PKG w/mult components, so no single portal.  Disc CirrusMD, WHLC, etc.
     - Went to MAP together so she could see how to sign in, & did super basic desc of what avail, but made sure she can see the Assistance ph #.  Let her know about the depth, calling for assist, etc.
     Basically, I encouraged her to feel free to always call the Conc Line as an initial GPS to her plan.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-23 13:07:13', '2022-09-23 13:07:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103833033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109180012', 'Cameron Sutter', NULL, 'I won''t give him a call until close to next month''s deadline, he said his wife needs to review the plan as well, from the looks of it he seems certain once his blue shield insurance term ends he will be enrolling with us for december or november. I don''t want to pressure him as he could be a center of influence so I''ll leave some time for him to enroll.', 'Tony Manzanarez', 'Tony Manzanarez', '2022-09-23 12:49:43', '2022-09-23 12:49:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103904018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093918002', 'Jennifer McMullen', NULL, '9.23.22 - Jennifer called because her daughter received a soccer injury and has been seeing the university doctor. The university doctor is now asking that her daughter have a knee MRI; I told Jennifer via phone what the fair price for a knee MRI w/ and w/o contrast is in Dubuque, IA. It is $1,359.00, I explained the self-pay process and advised Jennifer that if they ask for any payment for the MRI, to only pay the first $1,000 and ask that the rest be billed to her. I also explained how to open a need with Zion and sent her the instructions via email. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-09-23 12:29:25', '2022-09-23 12:29:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103910021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005676955', 'Hillary Harris', NULL, '9-23-2022:  Hillary called in.  She was in a great place today, so I did quite a bit of education w/her.  Went over the following components:
     - We got CirrusMD set-up on her smartphone.  Talked about good place to start if not an emergency, their hours, avail while traveling, limited antibiotics, how to "talk" instead of texting (per her question), & generally how to utilize this component.
     - ''P''lantin = ''P''reventitive ONLY.  Never use this card for anything else.  Went over doc off keeping on file = beware, if they bill this could be more than a ''cash-pay'' price.
     - Healthshare comp = Zion:  catastrophic, 1k IUA = issue spec, resp for 3/yr, 4th & bey.  Talked spec about an issue she''s having with a bubble (or cyst?) on her eye.  Is it considered "medical", then what to do if so.  Deadline for sub, ongoing = no 12mos or > to stay w/same IUA.  Save pymt receipt, det rec w/med coding, and to call us before 6mos deadline (I sugg no > 4 mos) & we will help her learn how to sub a ''med need''.
        With her migranes, she''s finding succ w/chiro & wanted to know if she can get help w/that.  We went over all details on chiro: maint not cov, part of a larger need, must be pre-appr & how to go about getting that prior appr.
        Care Conn:  surgery came up so I briefly went over help for non-emerg proc.
     - WHLC:  she''s wanting to get a discount of vision.  We got her reg & all we see is the lasik info.  Since they updated this site though, I''m not finding the search mode for diff services working.  It seems to be hit or miss.  She asked about chiropractic & I showed her how to find those disc.
     - MAP:  went over the counseling avail & basics of pattern, etc.  What else is avail on this site & its depth.  Assistance # = good help for this comp during bus hours.
     - Uber Doc:  she asked about this so we went over what this is & how it works.
     - Let her know there are many other comp:  Hosp Fin Assistance, HCBB, etc.  She agrees, she start just calling the concierge line to get guidance (she agrees the website & all the typing is diff on both ends).
     * I forgot to mention our pharmacy discount help...  Next time.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-23 12:24:57', '2022-09-23 12:33:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103910016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103573008', 'Jacob Needham', NULL, '9-23-2022:  Sharon Needham called saying she had signup her grandson inaccurately?  Use her name instead of her grandson''s...  I put her thru to Patti''s line since she''d know what to do.  Then after the call I decided to try to find a file & found this!  I''m not sure if it''s already been corrected, or if she didn''t do things wrong, or?  She said she''d already tt Jackie & cc (told her I''m not sure, maybe they work for her advisor Louis Spatafore?).  She seemed a bit confused in general, but was very nice.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-23 12:24:50', '2022-09-23 12:24:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103915003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005676955', 'Hillary Harris', NULL, 'Hillary has reached out to me again, she emails me from time to time asking questions on how certain thing will work, certain things that might be shared or not, if so how, etc. Today she emailed me asking if during her regular Ear Check-Up exam, if something is found or discovered, which she thinks something has been, what will happen and if she is responsible to pay her $1000 IUA out of pocket.  I replied to her say that Yes, she is correct in the fact that if something is found or diagnosed during her Ear Exam, then she is to pay ONLY her $1000 IUA out of pocket. After she has done that she is to ask to be billed the rest of the billing, if the bill(s) add up to being more than her $1k IUA. If the bill(s) are more, then once she is given the remaining bill(s) and has her receipts of paying the $1k, she is to contact Zion Health and open what is called a "Need" with a Needs case worker. That case worker will help her from there and guide her on what he next steps are. I gave Hillary Zion''s phone number and told her to call them after she gets my email and explain to them exactly what she told me. Zion will be able to help her from there and she will be all set. I explained that Zion will 100% share the rest of the costs after she met her $1k IUA and everything is approved. It is a very simple process and Zion gets in contact with her Ear provider she went to, directly and payment is processed between each other. Hillary does not need to negotiate or be the middle mad. Zion handles everything, which gives Hillary a sense of relief that everything is being taken cared of and she doesn''t need to worry about much. All set for now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-09-23 12:00:56', '2022-09-23 12:00:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103910011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000099369002', 'Hannah Roberg', NULL, '9-23-2022:  Hannah called.  She is getting health "ins" through her emp starting 10/1/2022.  I can''t tell who an advisor would be on this so I went ahead &amp; sent the cancellation form link &amp; told her someone may reach out, but it''s just a formality.  She will take care of this today - she understands we are getting super close to the end of the month.  Sent Patti a Teams chat to give her a heads up.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-23 11:46:54', '2022-09-23 11:46:54'),
