  ('zcrm_1579374000103364103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083541002', 'Kara Hollingsworth', NULL, 'Member submitted Cancellation request after speaking with Mike.  She will be getting benefits thru Spouses employer.  I will notify Planstin &amp; cancel billing.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-09-19 12:36:58', '2022-09-19 12:36:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000103385003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063240002', 'Ryan Cyphert', NULL, 'Ryan called in and said this is his first time utilizing his plan here with us, and stated that he has just been informed by his Primary Care provider, that he may possibly need to have his Gallbladder removed. He wanted to know the process and what he needs to do. I explained to him about using his IUA of $2500, presenting himself as a Cash Paying customer at whichever provider he goes to of his choice, due to there being no network he needs to stay in for Injury/Illness. I told him about that fact that he needs to contact Zion Health, who is his MCS provider, for this exact type of situation. I told him they are the ones that after he pays and meets his IUA, then all and any bills thereafter, he is to submit his proof of paying his IUA of $2500, ask the provider to bill him the rest, submit those bills into Zion, and start what is called the Need Process with Zion. I emailed him the explanation of that all works, it has the link to the place he starts the Need Process and submit his bills, lastly Zion''s support number is at the bottom as well and to call them asap to explain everything he told me. 

They will get him connected with a Case worker for his Need he will possibly be starting in the near future. He thanked me and said all of that makes perfect sense, is easy, and looking forward to my email. Ryan will call Zion the second he gets their contact info from my email I sent him. Then Ryan asked how we all work and what the difference is between us and Zion. He hit the nail on the head when he asked if we are like the umbrella of everything and members start with us first always, we will direct them to whomever, send whichever info they may need help with, etc. He understood. Lastly he asked after I started explaining Planstin and Ryan''s & Families Secure Plan they have and how his Preventative portion works, he stopped me and said that they actually do not need that at all and wouldn''t use the Preventative portion of their plan. Ryan said they are all very healthy people and never go to the doctors. I told him that is no problem at all and what he needs to do is contact Jane Kassel, his Healthcare Advisor who enrolled him and his family in the plan, and explain exactly what he told me about being healthy and won''t need or use the Planstin portion, I told him she can certainly tell him about our Care+ plan, which is exactly everything he already has EXCEPT the Preventative portion of the plan. 

He said he only needs what he used, the Injury/Illness catastrophic type of coverage. I told him Care+ is exactly that, along with the fact that switching to Care+ will save them a ton of money as well. He loved hearing about everything and is very very happy with the help he received here today. All set for now and has all the info he needs for his Gallbladder situation and to contact Jane Kassel about switching to Care+. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-09-19 12:12:11', '2022-09-19 12:12:32'),
