  ('zcrm_1579374000102932018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000102938002', 'James Cotter', NULL, '9-13-22 James is enrolling now. I reminded him that the insurance card is ONLY for his annual wellness visit and HSA compliance and he will be self-pay for everything else.  He''s good with that. He''s healthy and not pre-x to report. Enrolling in SECURE $1000/$300 EO, Oct. 1st, 2022 start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-09-13 16:43:44', '2022-09-13 16:43:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102932013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059112004', 'Salt Garrison', NULL, '9-13-22 Salt called and he wants to cancel bc of the price increase. He believes he can find something for much cheaper. I asked him if he does annual wellness visits and says sometimes. We will talk tomorrow about possible downgrade or changes to his membership. Price went from $275 to $325 per month.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-09-13 16:06:07', '2022-09-13 16:06:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102933018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740251', 'Evan Altman', NULL, '9-13-2022:  A man named Evan Altman called from caller ID #: (770) 394-6466.  He said someone keeps calling & LMs about our healthcare, but he''s on Medicare & doesn''t need any, so could we plez stop calling.  Leo is going to help me touch base w/the inhouse team members to make sure everyone knows, since I''m not seeing a ''Lead'' by this name, just this single ''Contact'' in the CRM.
     Leo thought maybe we have someone spoofing & using our #.  It just seems like an awfully large coinsidence that they''d be spoofing to one of our old members using our #.     
     Evan knows I''m trying to figure out who is calling.  If it continues, he will listen to the VMs again & give us the name the person is leaving in the message.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-13 15:25:01', '2022-09-13 18:07:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102933013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091091016', 'Daniel Rife', NULL, '9-12-2022:  Jody called.  She needed to adjust a few items on her RX Quotes so she can pickup some different RXs.
     - Midodrine - she didn''t pick it up when I sent the coupons in Aug. & her doc may chg the RX or take her off of it entirely when she sees him this month.  Therefore, I sent a revised coupon:
        Midodrine 5mg tabs, #30 = $14.52 @ Hy-Vee on GoodRX.
     - Dan''s:  Crestor (Generic = Rosuvastatin) - Brand is expensive, so I sent a generic coupon:
        Rosuvastatin 10mg tabs, #90 = $9.81 on RXSaver
[Both were slightly cheaper on other disc sites.  Midodrine was $14.29 on WellRX & the Rosuvastatin was ~$8.41 on PharmacyCkr (?), so a total of about $1.60 less.  However, those two coupons do not feature the Hy-Vee logo, so for the price diff, I went w/coupons that do.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-13 15:24:49', '2022-09-13 18:10:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102932008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810847', 'Sally Hammond', NULL, '9-13-22 Sally wanted to understand the changes taking place due to conversion with Sedera. But, they don''t have any open Needs either, only an old one from about 1 year ago. She thinks she received an email from Sedera about the conversion which she will look for and forward to me. If so, I''ll ask Sedera and MPB to close out the old need so she won''t have to convert until Jan. 1st 2023.  She also asked about dental, vision and hearing options. They don''t currently have an issues though. So, I shared the HMA with her and she likes the idea for perhaps the future if/when they anticipate expenses. They pay cash for all of those items now. She was super appreciative. They are temporarily living in NM now while friends live in their home here as their friend''s home is being renovated. So, they''re having fun spending time in Taos, NM!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-09-13 15:22:12', '2022-09-13 15:22:12'),
