  ('zcrm_1579374000102795003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077371001', 'Linda Blake', NULL, '9.12.22 - Linda & Donald called in with questions as to why "us people" told her that a physician she went to for her preventative care was in the PHCS network when the office staff just called her after her appointment to say that he was not in the network. She said that since "us people" told her that the physician is in the network, that we should pay the bills she''s receiving. Upon further discussion, it was stated that when Linda called the doctors office to make her appointment and used the information I gave her to make her appointment, the office staff told her that the physician is in the network and does accept Planstin. Donald insisted that "we people" needed to reimburse them for the bills that they have received from the provider. I explained that if the office told her prior to her appointment that the physician is in the network, then they would need to call the office and speak with them about this issue. But I reiterated that if the doctor IS NOT in the network, there is no reimbursement for that bill.  I am sending Linda and Donald lists of OBGYN''s and PCP in the network. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-09-12 09:37:12', '2022-09-12 09:41:39'),
