  ('zcrm_1579374000102747024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081920003', 'James Platt', NULL, '9/10/2022:  James is upset by the new age banded pricing &amp; threatens if we can''t keep it at the same price he might as well go w/his emp ins.  I sent e-mail going over benefits of an IUA (max on the qual iss is his 1k IUA, not annually either if ongoing) &amp; MPB.Health.  Incl the newest Memb &amp; Maternity Guidelines, highlighted some other components &amp; offered to find a time to discuss next wk if he''d like.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-10 16:19:13', '2022-09-10 16:19:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102747019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086537002', 'Katherine Kavich', NULL, '9-7-2022:  Sent Katherine 2 coupons re: RX Quote.  She prefers the Rite Aid in LaCanada, CA, which is considerably more expensive, but I always let her know her options & she still seems to prefer paying the higher price to go there.  Here''s what I sent:
     - Lininopril 5mg tabs, #90 = $14.96 on GoodRX for the LaCanada Rite Aid.  
        [Cheapest = $6.56 at Ralph''s on RXGo]
     - Fluticasone (she has BRAND, but this is a generic name) 50mcg, 1 nasal spray = 16g = $15.14 at LaCanada Rite Aid on GoodRX.  Coupon shows if she signs-up she can get a 1x discount & pay $10.14)
[Cheapest price = $11.04 at Ralph''s - didn''t mark which site, oops.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-10 14:10:22', '2022-09-10 14:10:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102747014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064604206', 'Patricia Moran', NULL, '9-2-2022:  Patricia e-mailed back she doesn''t have any Harris Teeter stores near her.  Sent her a new coup, where the retail on Climara is exactly as stated above (same retail price &amp; everything);
     - Progesterone 100mg caps, #90 = $25.21 at Winn Dixie on RXGo 
        Let her know if she does not have Winn Dixies near her, we can go to the 3rd cheapest, but the prices do continue to increase.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-10 14:02:46', '2022-09-10 14:02:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102747009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100500010', 'Brian Myers', NULL, '9-9-2022:  Brian & I talked about his RXs.  His pref pharmacy Walgreen''s best pricing is: $335.63.  Fry''s has 2 items w/contracted discount sites & he''s going to see if they will honor the 3rd (for his Methylphenidate ER) at the coupon price we found for other Frys locations, for a total of: $113.85.
     At first he was thinking these prices were high, but we are doing a 90ds (not 30) so he felt better about that.  His Methylphenidate ER (cont sub) could prove challenging.  It''s at best $82-$92, but most sites are quoting w/coupons $200-$300+.  He will ask the pharmacist to call the RXGo 1-800 # if they say they are not contracted to see if they can work something out.  He doesn''t need this item for about 10-14 days, so he''ll call me next week if we need to find another coup & knows the others are higher.
     Here are the 3 coupons I sent:
          - Lisinopril 40mg tabs, #90 = $9.03 at Sngl Care (no sign-up)
          - Tamsulosin 0.4mg caps, #90 = $11.10 on WellRX
          - Methylphenidate ER 54mg tabs, #90 = $90.73 at Frys (his Frys is not listed as contracted w/RXGo)  He''s going to try.  Walmart shows a cheaper price, but we were trying to get everything at the same place: $81.16 on RXGo - in case we need to get this item elsewhwer.)     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-10 13:49:21', '2022-09-10 13:49:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102732032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095959020', 'Mickey Chupek', NULL, '9-9-2022:  Brooke sent chat via SalesIQ ~ 5:50pm Friday night.  She totally does not know what her healthcare is about, who Planstin is, etc.  She is going to call next week so Jennifer or I can go over the basics, incl sending another ''Welcome Call'' invite.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-09 17:58:48', '2022-09-09 17:58:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000102732024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004762035', 'Traci Hoops', NULL, '9-9-2022:  A call from this caller id # (I''m assuming it was Traci herself), was asking for instructions on how to fill out the form for her daughter''s college.  I explained both Zion &amp; Planstin will provide "Proof of Benefit" letters she can submit with the info to prove she has healthcare.  I made sure she has both their ph #s.  She was grateful for the information.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-09-09 16:01:17', '2022-09-09 16:01:17'),
