  ('zcrm_1579374000101790031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082154002', 'Julia Fathe', NULL, '8.29.22 - Julia emailed in requesting to cancel her membership. I forwarded the email to Jane Kassel, her agent, so that she can get the cancellation process started for Julia. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-08-29 14:05:08', '2022-08-29 14:05:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000101790023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610171', 'Melinda Grabau', NULL, '8.29.22 - Melinda called in because she had opened a Medical Need with Zion regarding her husbands recent issues with memory loss, walking in his sleep, doing things in his daily life unknowingly, etc. Dr. Jeff Lee had determined that because he had seen both a Neurologist and a Cardiologist, that these should be two separate Needs because he didn''t think the symptoms went hand in hand. The Cardiologist wrote a letter for the Grabau''s stating that they do go hand in hand. She was advised by Wendy to call the concierge team so that we could advocate on her behalf. I had to explain to Melinda that the concierge team DOES NOT advocate for our members with Zion Health and we cannot go against any decisions that they have made. But what I could do is give her information on how to submit a detailed appeal for this incident. Melinda states that she was told by Wendy that we could do the appeal for her, but we also cannot do that from our side of things, the member has to do that themselves. I called Zion Healthshare and spoke with Eden who stated that there was no formal appeal filed by Melinda for her husband''s situation and that it was Dr. Jeff Lee would had made that final determination for that Need.  Eden then said to have Melinda file a formal appeal with the letter from the Cardiologist attached ASAP and they will get it over to Dr. Jeff Lee to see if there may be another determination in the Grabau''s favor. I followed up with Melinda via phone who stated that she is sick of Zion and how they determine what Needs are shareable. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-08-29 14:00:06', '2022-08-29 14:01:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000101832047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079422002', 'Aaron Handler', NULL, '8/29/2022:  Aaron wrote that the one thing they tried to claim was denied & so much wasn''t covered, the price increase means other companies are viable options.  I replied, offering to see why they were declined, because w/out details, it''s hard for me to know.  Also let him know I went over w/Shari how to get reimb on minimally the back-to-school physicals.  Sugg they use the Concierge Line like traffic directors to utilize the plan in the best manner.  Also mentioned w/the HSA eligibility, I find many of my members like this for that reason if nothing else.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-08-29 13:35:30', '2022-08-29 15:20:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000101832042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086854001', 'Ronald Olibas', NULL, '8-29-2022:  Rob says he''s being charged by us twice ea month.  One is ~ $330 &amp; he''s cking, but the second is $35-$40.  I trans him to Patti''s line &amp; he will LM if she cannot ans.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-08-29 13:35:23', '2022-08-29 13:35:23'),
