  ('zcrm_1579374000099280003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034059166', 'Deanna Johnson', NULL, '7.28.22 - Deanna called in (after previously speaking to Cari and not mentioning this specific situation) regarding a screening mammogram bill she received in the mail. She does not feel that she should be responsible for this bill and was demanding that someone pay it besides her. Deanna had switched plans as of June 1, 2022 from the Partially Self-Directed plan to the Secure plan. Deanna had a screening mammogram done in May 2022 and had it billed to RCI/APEX who denied payment for this mammogram due to the fact that she had one done the previous year. RCI/APEX only allows screening mammograms every other year. Deanna stated that her advisor, Andrea Hinman, never explained that when she switched plans that she would have a different MEC for her preventative services. Andrea would have relayed this information to the member, there is no doubt in my mind. I have emailed Andrea Hinman with this information and I am awaiting a response to see if Andrea would like to speak with Deanna about this prior to me doing her welcome call this afternoon. I am more than willing to explain this to Deanna myself, but I would like the advisor to make that decision. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-07-29 07:19:10', '2022-07-29 07:20:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154157', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002887157', 'Trevor Mickelson', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Julia called:
     - She thinks her husb is suffering from a mental breakdown.  We talked about the MAP counseling option, but she thinks he needs a psychiatrist (an MD, so thought maybe it would be cov).  We looked up the curr Zion Guidelines & read them together.  They have some info she found helpful
     - Also discussed medications.  She was excited to hear we may be able to find her better prices. 
     - It seems like we went over 1 other item, but the phones were so busy I''m trying to doc at the end of the day and am not sure what that was.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 18:09:35', '2022-07-28 18:09:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154152', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032016379', 'Maurine Killough', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Maurine called re: some e-mail she rec''d.  Saying we sent it and asking why I didn''t know anything about it.  Let her know I''m unaware of anything we sent, but that doesn''t mean anything since I''m in a diff dept.  Asked if it came from Zion as they sent a newsletter lately, but she can''t find it so said, nevermind on that.
     - We went over something else in depth, but the day was crazy & I cannot remember at this moment what it was (trying to document at the end of the day).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 18:08:37', '2022-07-28 18:08:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154144', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069838046', 'Brian Dotson', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Brian called to see if he has chiropractic options.  He has bursitis in his shoulder.  After tt CirrusMD, they thought a laser treatment thru the chiro office would be a good option.  We disc:
     - the WHLC disc & went online together to make sure he could access those.  Doc he''s interested in actually offers a 20% disc.
     - Discussed he has a $2500 IUA, so is ''cash-pay'' to that point.  I sugg: when he goes for initial appt, get ''Treatment Plan''.  IF this could linger, or continue, is going to be near his $2500 IUA, we may want to submit the ''Treatment Plan'' to see if Zion would pre-approve the chiropractic care.  Made it clear it must be pre-approved and they would only share past his $2500 IUA.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 18:01:06', '2022-07-28 18:01:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154139', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084183012', 'Ruth Jackson', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Ruth called, she''s trying to sub the ''medical need'' for her husb''s issue.  We walked thru the site &amp; I trans her at the end to Zion to get her ''Memb #''.  She seemed to have a good grasp on how to do this, what to include, etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 17:55:21', '2022-07-28 17:55:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010331067', 'Tessa Manton', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Wendy e-mailed, fwding Tessa''s concern: when her MD office calls the ph # on the back of her ins card to verify her coverage, they tell them she was terminated.  (Maybe they are using an old ASI Card?).  She''s requesting a new card.  But:
     - In Wendy''s notes, due to Covid, Tessa chose to go w/NO MEC.  (see Wendy''s note on 7/24/2020)
     - (Then again, see Wendy''s note on 3/3/2022) Wendy went over both NO MEC & how to handle appointments.
     - Thought this might be best for Wendy to address, so sent a reply to Wendy only:  
            ~ Not sure what card she wants us to order.
            ~ Included both notes mentioned so Wendy can refer to them as she goes over w/Tessa again how her plan works & the fact she chose no MEC.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 17:14:44', '2022-07-28 17:14:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000087122002', 'Robert Chupek', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Bob called.  When he rec''d the List Bill this mo, it''s showing a 1k IUA, but sb a 5k IUA.  It''s after hours, so he''s LM for Karina in accting.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 16:39:06', '2022-07-28 16:39:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154124', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993160', 'Karen Peirson', NULL, '7-28-22 Asking about the pre-x clause and her thyroid issue. Her membership began Jan. 1st 2019. So, she''s outside of the pre-x clause with Sedera at this point.  Responded to her email.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-07-28 16:36:11', '2022-07-28 16:36:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154119', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078240001', 'Samuel Haefner', NULL, '7-28-2022:  Samuel called - he needs a refill on his RX.  He''s been paying $9 for a 30-day supp on his old ins, but I was able to find a 90-day supp coupon for:  Sertraline (= Gen Zoloft) 50mg., #90 at Kroger Pharmacy on WellRX for $10.83.  E-mailed him the coup.
     [Note:  CostPlus w/shipping was only $11.70.  He may try that when he has time for shipping  /  Also Tom Thumb was his 2nd choice for local pharmacies &amp; w/$5 1st fill disc = $11.65, then I found for 2nd fill &amp; on 12.58]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-07-28 16:02:04', '2022-07-28 16:02:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000099154111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111063013', 'Stephanie Hoffman', NULL, '7-28-22 Talked with Stephanie and she''s been researching Zion directly with their prices for DPC and some add-ons. Now that their prices are cheaper, she''s wanting to work with me but not really wanting to pay the higher prices for all of MPB''s services. So, I quoted her the CARE+ membership price now, but it looks to be higher still than Zion. I''m going to check Zion''s prices to compare and see what''s best for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-07-28 15:21:35', '2022-08-01 14:26:54'),
