  ('zcrm_1579374000096006003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073951263', 'Christina LeBoeuf', NULL, '6.21.2022 - Christina called because she is having a yearly skin cancer check (which she hasn''t had since she''s had her plan) and wanted to know what was covered. I explained that it is not something that she would use her Planstin card for as it is not a preventative service, but that she would present herself as a cash-pay patient and keep the receipts in case this goes above her $1000 IUA amount. Christina wanted to know how she could get around that and have it all paid for by Planstin. I explained, again, that it is not a preventative service and offered to go over the list of preventative services with her. She kept asking how she could get around this issue and have it paid at 100%. Christina was not willing to take my answers, and stated that she was not sure why she even had this "insurance" if it is not going to pay for anything. I advised her to speak with Mike Montes and transferred her over. She just could not understand that there is absolutely no way to get around the fact that dermatology is not a preventative service. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-06-21 07:58:19', '2022-06-21 07:58:19'),
