  ('zcrm_1579374000095802003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000009604129', 'Lori Frisbie', NULL, '06/17/22 Call from Lori Frisbie to talk with Joan per Jane Kassel who told her to call and discuss an important benefits issue and a possible appeal with Sedera. Will have Joan call when she is available. AC', 'Alison Cary', 'Alison Cary', '2022-06-17 07:18:18', '2022-06-17 07:18:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000095766048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044571065', 'Anna Menz', NULL, '6-16-2022:  Anna called w/questions regarding use of her plan.  I tried calling Redirect &amp; just kept getting a busy signal.  I LM for her, letting her know I''ll follow-up.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-06-16 18:05:23', '2022-06-16 18:05:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000095766034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005667149', 'Tonya Cauduro', NULL, '6-16-2022:  Follow-up on the 6/10/22 issues.  I called Tonya, but she wasn''t in a place to do this, so I''m documenting a ton here for when she''s ready.  "Tonya has the few ''prev'' coverages thru her Zion plan = ''prev'' colonoscopy, mamm, & 1 ann visit" = from 6/10/22 note:

     - Re:  Mammogram on July 13, 2021.  I tt Grace in the ''Need'' Dept at Zion.  Tonya may normally pay $99 for her mammogram, but, when she tried using her Zion benefit for her annual mammogram, the provider billed Zion $988!  The doc at that time was in the PHCS Ntwk they were using, so the ntwk adj''d price was $889.20.  The mamm limit is $600/yr.  Therefore, the balance Tonya was billed was > than the $99 she normally pays.
       How to get around this:  When Tonya makes her mamm appt, ask how much it will cost (as a ''cash-pay'' pt without insurance).  Then call Zion ahead of your appt.  They will sent her a sngl use cc to use to pay for the mammogram.  So, if it''s normally $99, that''s considerably less than their max of $600 for a mamm, so she''ll pay nothing herself.

     - Re: Her ''prev'' annual appt.  She has a sngl appt each yr that she can choose to utilize her (excerpt from Zion''s Memb Guidelines directly today - not limitations!):
          "1. Annual Provider Visit
                 Annual provider visits are shareable upon membership activation, and may be used for preventive visits, specialist visits, or other services as outlined in the Preventive Medical
Sharing Guide. Zion Health will share the member’s first qualifying submission; all other
subsequent provider visits are the member’s responsibility until 12 months have passed since the qualifying visit.
                Any additional services provided at the time of service will be considered the member’s responsibility, including x-rays, labs, and other services. For these services, members may
seek lower cost options such as online or independent lab facilities by presenting as self-pay
patients. Members should take advantage of the Medical Advocacy Service as a complementary resource to help them locate low-cost facilities."
                This excerpt addresses her question about lab work w/her annual appt.  See the 2nd paragraph.

     - Re: Colonoscopy - This has severe limitations.  I didn''t get a great answer on how to handle this one.  I would suggest her calling Zion''s ''need'' dept for guidance on how to make sure this is paid for.  Previously, I''ve been told w/this particular benefit, they will try to keep it as a ''prev'' item if it''s the first time so it stays no IUA to the member.  What I do not know:  Will they move this to a ''need'' for the member if the balance goes drastically over their max for this benefit (like the mammogram)?  I planned to tell her Zion will work w/her to get her the lowest expense on this item, but we did not get to have our conversation.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-06-16 17:11:32', '2022-06-16 17:23:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000095766026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012630194', 'Frances Primus', NULL, '6-16-2022:  Frances called, she thought she had started a claim with us.  I went over Zion is her healthsharing component to her membership and since we are not ins, it looks like it''s a ''need'' that was started with them.  I made sure she had their ph #, went over using ext 5 = ''need'' dept, and trans her directly to them so they can guide her.  She was very nice, very sweet, and really appreciated my help.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-06-16 14:55:58', '2022-06-16 14:56:57'),
