  ('zcrm_1579374000093232003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017243184', 'Mark Capsalors', NULL, '05/13/22  St Francis Hospital called regarding Mark Capsalors benefits. I transferred him to Sedera to speak to directly. AC', 'Alison Cary', 'Alison Cary', '2022-05-13 07:40:41', '2022-05-13 07:40:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077866084', 'Judith Snyder', NULL, '5-12-2022:  Judy is super frustrated that there are no in network mammography centers w/in 1-1/2 h drive, even though she''s surrounded by centers.  Says "this is enough to make me change plans".  We disc options.  Finally she decided to contact her normal center to make sure they are not a PHCS Netwk facility & she has PHCS''s ph # if she needs to call them to see if they see any other options as well.  It seemed to help when I let her know I''d notify my supervisor of her frustration.  I sent Joan an informational Teams chat so she knows we have another member struggling w/this.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-05-12 17:21:51', '2022-05-12 17:21:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093223003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601108', 'Kevin Fechtmeyer', NULL, 'May 12th, 2022 - Marginne Tellez: Mrs. Sarah Pyper reached me through Sales IQ and she wanted to know how it will work if she takes her daughter to her regular pediatrician. I explained to her that she can take her to her pediatrician and based on the plan that your ex-husband has, he has an HSA card which means that he can use it o most clinics and hospitals and in the country as long as it is a medical-related cost.', 'MPB Southern District Agents', 'MPB Southern District Agents', '2022-05-12 17:21:26', '2022-05-12 17:21:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081460002', 'Hollie Snow', NULL, '5-12-2022:  Hollie''s advisor Traci sent me a Teams chat.  Hollie provided her Planstin card to get a preventative mammogram, but it was declined because the provider is not in network.  Traci knows they talked about this prior to Hollie becoming a memb, but thinks she forgot w/the time gap.  She also thinks she told Hollie to connect w/the Concierge Team, but I''m not seeing any notes.  Traci & I disc options for pymt via HSA, etc.  She''s going to try to help Hollie & knows there''s not much we can do on a ''prev'' item on the backside.  I did ask if they saw anything & it moved from screening to diagnostic for a need?     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-05-12 17:18:42', '2022-05-12 17:18:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015647211', 'Jacqueline Woodward', NULL, '5-12-2022:   Jacqueline''s having to go thru more testing due to her high risk hormone/breast tissue issue.  Because she does not know how to separate the issues (they think a ton is linked), she''s going to upload the newest items towards the same ''need'', but she understand Zion may separate them if they are considered sep issues & we went over how IUAs work.  She will call Zion if it''s determined it''s a diagnostic item to confirm how payment will/will not be handled.
     - She has Planstin MEC, so we discussed ''prev'' vs diagnostic & the 2 entities (Planstin & Zion).  She may call Planstin to conf if her MRI will be a ''prev'' item since they are utilizing it on her because she''s high risk, or if it''s not, she realizes it will go twds her Zion ''need''(s).     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-05-12 17:08:46', '2022-05-12 17:08:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061691226', 'Dolores Pope', NULL, '5-12-2022:  Dolores called frustrated her COVID Test submitted to Zion was declined.  We talked about what is covered & what is not on her Care+ healthcare option.  She''s confused how this is a health plan if it''s not ins.  I recommended her advisor Zach Masters might be able to help there.  I sugg if she needs another Covid test, curr most states sill offer free tests & walked her thru how to handle it next time.
     - She also started a ''need'' w/Zion re: a ''prev'' mammogram.  But, it turns out they are questioning the images and doing more diagnostic testing.  I sugg she include the further items on this issue to that same ''need'' & tt her ''need'' counselor at Zion for guidance on how this will be handled, where she is on meeting her 1k IUA for this item, etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-05-12 17:03:13', '2022-05-12 17:03:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025330019', 'Carly Hayes', NULL, '5-12-22 Carly is taking her employers benefits now for June 1st because it''s cheaper for her. She will keep her Spirit Dental and VSP.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-05-12 16:03:02', '2022-05-12 16:03:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091076009', 'Jasmine Buckelew', NULL, '5-12-2022:  Jasmine called re: RX Quote she sub.  Needs the Norethindrone right away.  Disc could be free on Planstin ''prev'' medications, she doesn''t want to do that today.  Sent her first 2 coupons as follows (waiting for pricing from Reid on other two). Pricing for her chosen pharmacy = Kroger were both cheapest on RXGo today:
     Spironolactone 50mg., #120 @ Kroger = $13.40
     Norethindrone 0.35mg, #84 (=3 pkts) @ Kroger = $10.81     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-05-12 14:53:10', '2022-05-12 14:53:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000093193008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086830002', 'Tau Braun', NULL, '5-12-2022:  Jenn called.  They wanted to get a coupon so Tau can pickup his RX.  We went thru quite a few pharmacies & they decided CVS is most conv (w/a decent price).  Today RXGo had his Add 20mg, #90 for #31.60 (which was cheapest for CVS).  Sent the coupon.     - CA

