  ('zcrm_1579374000091982008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045889025', 'Laurie Testa', NULL, '4.29.2022 - Laurie called because she needed to cancel and had questions about her HSA but she could not reach her advisor, Daniel Zaborowski. I did try calling Daniel myself, but his number is no longer in services. I reached out to Daniels upline, Jan Capodi, and she will be reaching out to Laurie if she cannot get ahold of Daniel. JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-04-29 08:39:53', '2022-04-29 08:39:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091991003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034059166', 'Deanna Johnson', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online after start date of June 1, 2022. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2022-04-29 08:03:43', '2022-04-29 08:03:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091982003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442360', 'Whitney Hammond', NULL, 'Whitney called because his college aged son needs to get his Adderall refilled but has not found a doctor yet. He was wondering if the CirrusMD docs would fill his prescription. I advised Whitney that there are a few prescriptions, especially controlled substances, that the CirrusMD docs will not fill due to the risk of addiction or abuse and that Adderall may be one of them. I told him that he could reach out to the MAP program to see if they could give him some guidance on how to get this prescription filled as he is looking for a new doctor in his new area. I gave Whitney the MAP programs phone number and he was very happy with his service. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-04-29 07:57:53', '2022-04-29 07:57:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091962018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084812002', 'Hermilo Cavazos', NULL, '4-28-2022:  Hermilo called.  The tests on the baby came back positive.  They are seeing a specialist tomorrow & he''s presented his Planstin card again.  Reminded him that''s only for ''prev'' care which he seemed to remember once we discussed it again.  We went over starting his ''need'' now that they know this will require ongoing treatment. I can tell he''s overwhelmed, so I sent the temp for starting a ''need'' w/Zion again per his request.  I did let him know I''m concerned due to the timing:  Eff = 3/1/2022; baby born 3/14/2022.  However, did not say anything more because Zion should let him know if it''s not covered.  Not sure what was gone over w/his advisor prior to joining.
     [After getting off phone, I looked at Zion Guidelines.  As far as I can tell, this will be a pre-x item.  But, at least they may get some help after the 1 yr waiting period?]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-04-28 18:05:06', '2022-04-28 18:05:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091962013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078032313', 'Colette Krasnow', NULL, '4-28-2022:  Doing Dopler &amp; MRI due to issue that took her to ER.  Wanted to talk about process.  She tt Zion today, has signed the HIPPA form, &amp; they told her they are getting her records to make sure not a pre-x (she says it''s definitely not).  She''ll present as ''cash-pay'' minimally to the 1k IUA, but may go further if they req $ upfront on new tests. Then will upload new info to her curr need.  She seems to understand &amp; it looks like she has a good grasp on the situation.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-04-28 17:55:36', '2022-04-28 17:55:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091940008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082146002', 'Ursa Abernathy', NULL, 'I emailed member Payment Update Link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-04-28 17:00:33', '2022-04-28 17:00:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091962008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084814001', 'James Rosenow', NULL, '4-28-2022:  James wants to add a child(ren) to his plan.  Sent him Patti''s Plan Chg temp &amp; let him know start date may be 6/1/22 for changes made currently -- Patti can confirm that &amp; if there''s a new mo contribution for him.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-04-28 16:15:19', '2022-04-28 16:15:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000091963013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000092077036', 'Daniel Sosalla', NULL, '4-28-22 Spoke with Dan late on Tuesday. He''s losing coverage from work at end of April and needs May 1st start date. He''s given crappy ins through new job that won''t cover enough for him. Has an expensive med. "FYI, your buproprion XL is cheaper via mail-order on GoodRX than paying a $30 co-pay. However, the Vyvanse doesn''t have a generic. You may need to talk with your doctor to have them prescribe a similar generic drug, if possible.

"Vyvanse (lisdexamfetamine) is used to treat attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD). This drug is more popular than comparable drugs. There are currently no generic alternatives to Vyvanse."

This will wind up being too expensive if it''s considered a preferred brand drug with a $160 co-pay! Non-preferred they don''t even cover.

Most doctors will work with you on the medications to find something that works and is affordable."

He just called me now to learn how to show proof of Life Change Event and upload to docs. He will also work on calling dr. to get more affordable med in place of Vyvanse.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-28 15:48:30', '2022-04-28 15:48:30'),
