  ('zcrm_1579374000091093031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000067089037', 'Doug Durgee', NULL, '4-20-22 "My wife just got a job, so we need to weigh our insurance options again.

To recap you, I''m self-employed and made $70K last year (I believe it came to $40K after deductions), and we wound up going with a silver plan with Bright Healthcare paired with DPC. We''re mostly healthy, don''t visit the doctor that much other than checkups, so don''t need anything too fancy.

The wife is now making a W2 salary of $72K ($48K for the remainder of this year). The offered plan is a Gold POS plan for about $1100/mo ($1200 w/ dental/vision).

In our case I lean towards staying put, but I''m sure that the added income will affect our currently monthly premium. Can you advise? We have until tomorrow to decide on the wife''s option. If better to call, when are you available?

Thank you,
Doug Durgee
720-261-5346"

In looking over everything, their full cost without a subsidy will be $778.72 for their current Bright Health Bronze 5300 HSA and they chose Dr. Lee DPC for about $130 a month bringing the total to $908.72. They get the tax benefits and the unlimited care with Dr. Lee, plus save about $200 a month. So, they might stay put but they will discuss tonight and let me know. Total income will be about $129K with $57K for Doug and $72k for Dominic.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-20 14:34:07', '2022-04-20 14:34:07'),
