  ('zcrm_1579374000090760007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062380223', 'Aaron Pier', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 1567 Question : I''d like to know how I can set up an HSA and how to use the concierge service for medical expenses that are not shareable.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2022-04-13 13:44:45', '2022-04-13 13:44:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000090719021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086950002', 'Summer Deaton', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Summer seems confused about who MPB.Health is and who Zion Health is and the parts that they play. I tried to explain several times how all of the moving parts of her plan work, but she still did not understand and said she did not understand MY purpose. I explained that MPB.Health''s concierge team is a traffic director, we can answer most questions and address most issues, but there are times where we need to transfer you to either Zion or Planstin to receive the answer to a question. She kept stating that she did not understand my purpose and before I could finish her Welcome Call, asked to be transferred to Zion. She then asked, "Are you done?" to which I let her know that I was not done with her call quite yet, but I would be more than happy to transfer her to Zion if she would rather do that instead of finishing her call. She stated that I could hurry up and finish, then I could transfer her to Zion since I couldn''t answer her question. I finished and transferred her to Zion after she asked if I could reach out to Wendy with the following question: Is it beneficial for a child to have both a traditional insurance plan AND the medical cost sharing plan? ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-04-13 13:30:12', '2022-04-13 14:21:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000090792003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026122744', 'Kimberly Payes', NULL, '4-13-22 I explained to Kim why we switched her to MPB CareZ Bridge bc she was going to lose her MEC/wellness and HSA compliance and the age banding with Sedera was going to put her into a higher price bracket. Plus the added benefits of alternative care were in her favor and she got immediate sharing up to $25K for pre-x if she had any. Membership was not available to public. She''s psyched and happy to stay put. She recently did her colonoscopy and forgot to give Planstin card which she''s sorting out now. I let her know the PHCS network in Boulder County is fantastic, so that shouldn''t be a problem. She''s super sweet and happy. Dr. Tusek is her Dr. and he''s using Sedera which is why she doubted herself. Dr. Tusek really likes Sedera, which is great!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-04-13 11:34:46', '2022-04-13 11:34:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000090765008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991117', 'Ryan Dunlap', NULL, '4-13-2022:  Ryan called, he dislocated his elbow last week &amp; ended-up in the ER.  He told them he was ''cash-pay'' &amp; they brought the 8k bill down to 3k!  I sent him the temp to start a ''need'' w/Sedera &amp; went over the process.  He will have follow-up expenses too &amp; is aware he is resp for the $2500 IUA. 
 [Note for Cari:  Centaurus HS - late 90''s w/Wanekas]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-04-13 11:28:29', '2022-04-13 11:28:29'),
