  ('zcrm_1579374000089992023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '3-31-2022:  Wendy had Georgeanna give the concierge a call.  She''s wanting to see if PrimeHealth membership would be covered on her plan.  They are a membership type provider that look more into specific baselines, etc.  It will only be her, not her wife, that will have this membership, so a discount for a Direct plan isn''t an option, even if this membership fit the prev care side. 
    - I explained how alternative care must be linked to a specific ''need'' and pre-approved by Zion.  She''s wanting them to reimburse her on the backside.   I sugg if they find an issue, maybe PrimeHealth would be willing to breakout the expense of the tests, visits, etc., that are part of diagnosing and caring for the issue and she could submit it as a ''need''.  We talked about her 1k IUA.  
     - She lives near Dr Tusek, so I mentioned he might be a good fit.  She says they''ve tried to get into him & have never been able to because he''s so hard to get an appt with.  I mentioned Dr. Flannigan used to be his partner, so maybe has a similar philosophy?  She''ll think on this and move fwd.
     - At the end of our call, she decided she wanted to talk to Zion.  I made sure she has their # in case she needs to call them again and I trans her directly to them.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-31 17:30:09', '2022-03-31 17:30:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089992018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059563258', 'Brandi Stanley', NULL, '3-31-2022:  Brandi called.  She completely overwhelmed with how to handle things.  She was told to have her doctor''s office call to confirm her elig, they told her they don''t do that.  She used I''m part of a self-funded plan, they didn''t know what that meant.  I tried to make it a bit easier & at least got her to making her first prev appt w/an in network doc.
     - She conf via the PHCS search tool & the doctors office, the doc is part of the PHCS "MultiPlan" network.  We left it since she''s conf that, go ahead and make a purely ''preventative'' care appt.   When she arrives, she will present her Planstin care & point to the PHCS MultiPlan on the back to confirm they are still part of the Network.
     - We talked about labs that are/are not covered & that at every turn in the ''prev'' appt, remind the doc it needs to be in network (ie: labs, etc) and coded prev to be covered.  Even non-covered labs will kickback at a discounted Network rate.
     - She asked for when she is ready to do diagnostic/treatment, what does she do.  We discussed ''cash-pay, and if it goes over the first 1k IUA on specific item (kidney issue, sprained ankle, etc.) we need to start a ''need'' for a qualified item.  IF they ask about her Planstin since they have it on file, she''s going to tell them that is for her ''prev'' care only and will not apply to her diagnostic/treatment this time.
    - We talked about calling us if she needs to sub a ''need'' to Zion, timelines, and what would be involved.
She''s trying to take in a lot.  We left it make your ''prev'' appt.  Then feel free to call so we can help guide you as you move fwd.  That seemed to take some of the pressure off.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-31 16:44:56', '2022-03-31 16:44:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089992008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000048143018', 'AJ Chamberlin', NULL, '3-31-22 AJ has decided to cancel. Then Christian with Redirect just called me back to handle her case. UGH! 5 minutes too late. AJ has access as a realtor to some insurance plan through Cigna PPO that she says she''d only pay $100 for ER!  Not worth pressing. Redirect will sort out her bills and she will move onto to her other plan as of April 1st.
Per call with Christian, for her Jan. 20, 2022 BCH visit for mammo, they will pay the cost directly to BCH since she hasn''t paid yet, but received an erroneous denial letter. It will be paid. The pap screening she called in advance and was given the places to choose from. She had a $900 bill for wellness, thyroid and one other issue. Part of this should be paid for. Finally the colonoscopy he''s looking into as well and she did communicate with them prior as well. Too little, too late. :-(', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-31 15:22:46', '2022-03-31 15:22:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089992003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058781071', 'Dante Ali', NULL, 'Member called to ask about both Preventative &amp; Injury &amp; illness submission.  Kelly went through detailed explanation.  I also asked again for updated payment info.  Hopefully she will send.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-31 15:06:38', '2022-03-31 15:06:38'),
