  ('zcrm_1579374000089702003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089447002', 'Rebecca Gradler', NULL, 'Rebecca called in this morning and said she has a Welcome Call today at 1pm with Vanessa and wanted to know how to reschedule that. I transferred Rebecca over to Vanessa and Vanessa took the call to help Rebecca out &amp; reschedule. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2022-03-29 08:07:38', '2022-03-29 08:07:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089699003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058781071', 'Dante Ali', NULL, 'Member''s 4/22 payment declined 1st notice sent 3/29 also spoke to spouse she will let member know.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-29 08:05:25', '2022-03-29 08:10:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089679028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091189002', 'Sarrah Claman', NULL, '3-28-22 See Client Questionnaire attached.  Sounds like CARE+ will be the best for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-28 17:39:33', '2022-03-28 17:40:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089674063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079936010', 'Kelly Margerum', NULL, '3-28-2022:  Kelly called in.  We went over a ton, but when I got another call I realized as I was looking up that person, I lost my unsaved notes on Kelly.  
     - I just cannot remember what we talked about.  Too many calls ...     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-28 16:11:24', '2022-03-28 16:12:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089674058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044006639', 'Ashley Semidey', NULL, '3-28-2022:  Ashley called.  She''s been a member long enough she''s completely forgotten how this works.  She had a ton of questions:
     - They are trying to get pregnant, how does it work?*
     - They''ve seen doctor(s) for certain items, pd w/HSA, is it covered for reimb?  Discussed preventative vs ''need''.  She doesn''t think anything has been > than their 1k IUA (& it didn''t sound like anything was prev from what she said.  We talked about imp to start a ''need'' w/in about 4 mos (to beat any deadline) if looks like it could continue and go over IUA.*
     - I let her know on prev, it must be in network & billed by the doc office (no reimb, which is what she''s started asking about).
     - She asked about occupational therapy her daughter is having.  She''s 4 & was having issues in daycare. The doc sugg this therapist.  Disc might be if linked to medical ''need''.   But therapies connected to a ''need'' would req pre-approval (we found info in Sedera Access+ Guidelines that she agreed, doesn''t look like her daughter''s curr care would be cov.  She may conf directly w/Sedera.*
     - Went over MAP program & the counseling attached to that, how it works, how to access their site, & I gave her their assistance ph#.
     - She was still thinking in term of deductible.  Went over IUAs not the same, not ins, etc.  Her IUA is 1k.  This was a bit harder for her to comprehend.  Noticed there are 81 IUA entries in the guidelines, so she''ll read those.*

 * I showed her how to access Sedera''s Access Guidelines.  She was very astute & finding information she was looking for quite quickly.

I think that was everything...     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-28 15:57:00', '2022-03-28 15:57:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089679018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089685024', 'Brent Skinner', NULL, '3-28-22 Brent Skinner just enrolled in the HMA $20,000 to help pay for his current back issues. He has 5 bulging discs. His travel insurance from New Zealand ended around Jan. 10-12th. So, he''s past the open enrollment and any SEP time frames. His taxes will show about $60K for 2021. He will likely only claim$20K-$30K for 2022 but that won''t help for the new SEP and he already filed his taxes, so he can''t choose the SEP option. So, the HMA can help with future payments and possible surgery for his back even when he can get ins. It will help pay for the ded.  He also has his own small biz in case that helps. But, he only has contract workers and no employees, no intention of helping to pay, no real group to speak of. He is currently seeing chiro and some procedure he might get to help will cost him $800-$2800 cash. Cash will be the best way to pay for now until his HMA is built up enough to pay out of that account with cash as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-28 15:52:04', '2022-03-28 15:52:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089674053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069290213', 'Amy Bloom', NULL, '3-28-2022:  Amy called looking for what ph line she would have a friend call to find out about MPB.  I gave her instructions on how Wendy Scipione likes to have referrals done:  Send e-mail to her friend &amp; cc WendyS@mympb.com, giving Wendy''s name &amp; ph to her friend in the e-mail.  This way, Wendy has a way to see who the referral came from as well.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-28 15:38:35', '2022-03-28 15:38:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089679013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045438013', 'Drew Cifrodelli', NULL, '3-28-22 I talked with Drew and gave him the price to add his twin sons who will be turning 18 this year. It will be $610/$1500 on PDHC which he said is more expensive then if they just stay put. So, he won''t add them. He has a Careington card and hasn''t had success in using it or via the # on the card. I''m not sure if Redirect or Sedera would provide that card. I didn''t think that was included in either company''s offerings. I''ve sent a not to Patti to see if she knows. He needs 2 crowns done in the next bunch of months. His dentist charges $2800 and he wants to shop around to see if he can find anything better.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-28 15:20:07', '2022-03-28 15:20:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089674048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086926010', 'Theresa Staiano', NULL, '3-28-2022:  Theresa''s employer wants/requires her to have a TB test.  She wondered if her plan would pay for that.  I went over Care+ is more for the larger expenses and does not have prev (I did not go into telehealth in this call).  She thinks they have a doc they may want her to see.  If not she''ll pick one &amp; we went over in detail ''cash-pay'' (to her $2500 IUA and if it looks like it will be near the $2500 she will have more to the process).  She seemed to understand pretty well.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-28 14:52:30', '2022-03-28 14:52:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089663100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081460002', 'Hollie Snow', NULL, 'Member requested payment update form.  I emailed.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-28 14:45:13', '2022-03-28 14:45:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089663095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027741246', 'Kristann Orton', NULL, 'I heard from this member that she never heard anything from either Leslie or Misty.  I will send her out cancellation link and cancel when I receive.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-28 14:23:29', '2022-03-28 14:23:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089663090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041829001', 'Kruti Patel', NULL, 'Per our research the group Total Healthcare was being billled out of Quickbooks.  Michele was told that they had cancelled Sedera eff 1/1/22 and did not tell us.  Cancelled as of 12/31/20', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2022-03-28 14:17:05', '2022-03-28 14:17:05'),
