  ('zcrm_1579374000089472008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081146002', 'Lisa Doughty', NULL, 'Lisa Doughty called with several questions about her plan. She has not had her Welcome Call as of yet so I highly suggested that she schedules one, and I sent her a new Welcome Call scheduler. She had originally called Zion Health about details of her plan, and they had told her that she does not have "insurance" (which is correct). So, I explained what each entity in her plan does and when to present her Planstin card. I did a mini–Welcome Call with Lisa. She then asked about her accident insurance that she purchased alongside her MPB.Health plan. She stated that Zion advised her that her accident insurance would take precedence for payments over her Zion plan. Lisa did not understand this concept, so I explained it to her to the best of my ability. I explained that her accident insurance would in fact, be the first to cover any payments for service and then, if it is still above her $1,000 IUA, that she would be responsible for her IUA and anything else would go to Zion for payment. She seemed to understand but will be scheduling a welcome call soon. ~JTS', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2022-03-24 09:36:32', '2022-03-24 09:36:32'),
