  ('zcrm_1579374000089434014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442111', 'Sarah Getzelman', NULL, '3-23-2022:  Sarah called re: her colonoscopy again.  She understands what we went over last time., but wanted to clarify how it works w/the diff entites needing to be in the PHCS MultiPlan network.  Then, she realized she''s had to have polyps rem''d in the past and wanted to clarify how it work then.  We talked about 1k IUA, network won''t matter at that point, and how to handle by starting a ''need''.  
     [When I looked at her start date, I was thinking she was brand new, but she''s actually been w/us a year so I tried calling her back to ask when the last colonoscopy was, to go over limitations.  If it was in the last year & they pulled polyps, maybe this is a follow-up and they won''t consider it preventative anyway?  However, no one answered & it was dead air.  No answering machine, etc.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-23 11:39:12', '2022-03-23 11:39:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089434003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059725045', 'Michelle Skellion', NULL, '3-23-2022:  Michelle''s son is on the track team & curr unable to run.  They think due to his extreem growth spurt he needs some alignment  thru chiropractic.  She wondered if that''s anything that might be shared.  We went over all alternative treatments need to be ''pre-approved''.  She''s going to get a treatment plan from the chiropractor & I sent her the temp to sub a ''need'' to Zion.  Once she''s sub it, she''s going to ask Zion if she can start paying towards the 1k IUA so they can start the treatment and still have them see she''s working for prior approval.  She''ll call if she needs further assistance.
     - At the end of the call, I could tell Michelle couldn''t hear me anymore and then we were disconnected.  Both Jennifer & I are experiencing weird things w/GoTo this week...  I tried calling Michelle back a few minutes later, but it went to VM & her box was full.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2022-03-23 11:28:02', '2022-03-23 11:38:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000089421011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089431001', 'Jessica Rapoza', NULL, '3-23-22 Jessica is on TriCare for only $300 annually, so she just wanted to understand how this works and if it was something worth exploring or not. But, she sees that her TriCare is worth keeping and covers her well enough at an amazing price. So, she will stick with it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2022-03-23 11:10:28', '2022-03-23 11:10:28'),
